app.log	1
app.log	2
-- a hard link is not read
app.log	3
-- a write through the other name is read under the read name
app.log	4
-- the read name is removed, and the other name is linked again and then removed: read on, not from the start
new.log	5
-- the same name is linked again
6
-- link and unlink: the only other name reads on
next.log	7
-- a hard link renamed into the directory is not read
next.log	8
-- the read name is replaced by another file: the other name reads on, the new file is read from the start
keep.log	10
next.log	9
-- a hard link made while the table is detached
keep.log	11
-- hard links and a symbolic link that exist when the table is created
a.log	1
a.log	2
-- a symbolic link that exists when the table is created
a.log	1
-- hard links and symbolic links to a read file are not read
a.log	2
-- the read name is removed: a hard link reads on, not a symbolic link
b.log	3
-- symbolic links that no longer point to the file do not keep it: a file linked back from outside the directory is read from the start
v.log	1
v.log	2
v.log	3
v.log	4
-- a symbolic link to a file outside the directory is read
z.log	5
-- a hard link to a file read under a symbolic link reads it on
y.log	6
-- the hard link is removed: the symbolic link reads on
z.log	7
-- a symbolic link that no longer points to the file does not keep it either when it is the read name
w.log	5
w.log	6
w.log	7
w.log	8
